myna-config (0.3.1-0ubuntu1) tenacious; urgency=medium

  * Teach Myna your words: add names and terms to the vocabulary in
    Myna Settings' Model tab, and the Parakeet model is far more likely
    to write them the way you did (#1). Whisper and FunASR do not use
    it yet.
  * Switching engine or model no longer leaves the old one's files on
    disk (#61).
  * Typing on Plasma Wayland keeps your keyboard layout during a
    dictation (#4).
  * Setting up Myna on Xfce and Plasma no longer stops at the indicator
    step until the next login (#79).
  * On Plasma with software rendering, the first dictation no longer
    stalls while the pill starts.

 -- Charles <charles05@canonical.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:55:35 +0000

myna-config (0.3.0-0ubuntu1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * KDE Plasma 6 is supported. Myna Settings sets up IBus as KWin's
    input method and binds the dictation key, and the pill shows on
    Plasma's Wayland session (#65, #79).
  * Notifications no longer pile up on Plasma (#70).
  * Long dictations into Wine and CrossOver applications are no longer
    cut off (#73).
  * Choosing a model while it is still installing no longer leaves Myna
    with no model (#51).
  * Myna Settings works when your shell is not listed in /etc/shells
    (#74).
  * Dictation ends cleanly when another input method takes over, and
    Myna claims IBus back at the next dictation.
  * The pill follows the desktop's accent colour and animation settings.

 -- Charles <charles05@canonical.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:36:17 +0000

myna-config (0.2.4-0ubuntu1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Myna runs on 64-bit Arm (arm64): Myna Settings from the PPA and
    every model from the Snap Store. Only basic testing has been
    performed. Testing from those with AArch64 setups would be much
    appreciated!
  * A microphone with a DC offset no longer keeps dictation running
    forever or hides its pauses, and Diagnostics shows the last
    dictation's input levels and warns about such an offset (#64).
  * Whisper and Parakeet finish a dictation on the CPU when the GPU
    runs out of memory partway through, instead of losing the text.
  * Whisper no longer silently skips long stretches of speech that have
    pauses in them.
  * New translations: Azerbaijani, Esperanto, Estonian, French, Occitan,
    Polish, Russian, Slovak, Ukrainian and Traditional Chinese.

 -- Charles <charles05@canonical.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:21:58 +0100

myna-config (0.2.3-0ubuntu1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * On an NVIDIA machine whose driver Myna cannot use, setup picks the
    CPU engine instead of the GPU one (#49).
  * A GPU engine that loses its driver keeps transcribing on the CPU and
    says so, instead of failing every dictation.
  * Myna tells you when dictation is slowed by low memory.
  * Report an Issue includes each model's engine and status even when
    Diagnostics was never opened.
  * An NVIDIA GPU older than the engine's CUDA libraries support, such
    as a GTX 1050, gets the CPU engine too, and a GPU that cannot start
    keeps transcribing on the CPU (#56).

 -- Charles <charles05@canonical.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:24:49 +0100

myna-config (0.2.2-0ubuntu1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Xubuntu support: Myna Settings sets up IBus and the dictation
    shortcut through Xfce's own settings, the dictation indicator runs
    on X11, and Settings follows a dark Xfce theme.
  * Setup recognises an installed machine on non-English desktops (#40,
    #50).
  * Setup recommends and installs the model for your language, and sets
    Whisper's spoken language to match.
  * Holding the dictation shortcut toggles once, and the first dictation
    after IBus starts finds the text field.
  * A missing IBus is reported in Diagnostics and Setup says why it
    cannot continue; recommend ibus and im-config.
  * A shortcut conflict names the application holding the key, not its
    command.

 -- Charles <charles05@canonical.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:25:05 +0100

myna-config (0.2.1-0ubuntu1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Setup speaks to screen readers: the download size, each install step,
    and focus moving on when it finishes. Thanks to Paul Geoghegan.
  * Changing the shortcut announces that it is waiting for a key, and why
    a key was refused.
  * Report an Issue in the main menu opens a GitHub issue with your
    diagnostics already filled in.
  * Diagnostics name the OS, desktop session and languages, and no longer
    freeze the window while they load.
  * Dictation recovers when IBus restarts with a new address.
  * The dictation indicator starts at the next login when Myna is
    installed mid-session.

 -- Charles <charles05@canonical.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:56:17 +0100

myna-config (0.2.0-0ubuntu1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Guided first-run setup: Myna Settings installs the Dictation app, a
    model and the Shell extension itself, under a single authorization
    prompt.
  * The Backend tab is now Model: switch models with one click, install
    more from within Settings with download progress, and get a
    recommended model for your language.
  * Settings apply the moment you change them; no confirmation dialogs.
  * Sound cues on start, stop and error, with a choice of sound sets
    previewed in Settings (Chime by default).
  * Whisper large-v3 and large-v3-turbo on NVIDIA GPUs.
  * A Diagnostics page that explains in plain words what is wrong and
    what the daemon last reported.
  * The ribbon HUD style is back; the error pill now meets WCAG AA
    contrast.
  * The dictation shortcut is a GNOME custom keybinding, captured inline
    in Settings. The portal shortcut and hold-to-talk are gone; the
    shortcut toggles dictation.
  * A model connected after login is picked up without restarting Myna.
  * A second dictation is spaced from the text before it.

 -- Charles <charles05@canonical.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 17:22:09 +0100

